---
import IndexLayout from '../layouts/IndexLayout.astro';
---

<IndexLayout title="About" description="A personal collection of mental models, mostly backend and infra, each with one interactive simulation.">
  <h1 class="text-[length:var(--fs-2xl)]">About</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    A collection of mental models, mostly backend and infra, and whatever else I need to hold in my head. Each one is a
    short explanation with one interactive model you can poke at.
  </p>
  <p>
    I keep these for myself first. When I have to reason about how a system behaves, I want a picture I can step through.
  </p>
  <p>
    The models are deliberately small. They leave out everything that does not change the point being made, and name the
    one or two things that do. Numbers on screen are the model's numbers, not measurements from a real system, unless an
    entry says otherwise.
  </p>
  <p>
    Made by <a href="https://iamit.in">Amit Kumar</a>.
  </p>
</IndexLayout>
